@startuml
title Recommendation request — session and retrieval decisions
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox

actor User
participant RequestGateway as Gateway
participant InputParser as Parser
participant SessionTransitionService as Transition
participant "ConversationEngine\nIntent handlers + RecommendationPager" as Engine
participant "SessionRepository\nRedis adapter" as Sessions
participant "RecommendationWorkflow\nEmbedding → retrieval → ranking" as Workflow
participant "ReadHistoryRepository\nOptional history adapter" as History
participant "ConversationResponseGenerator\nAI narration when needed" as Response

User -> Gateway : Natural-language request
Gateway -> Parser : parseUserIntent(text, lazy context supplier)
opt AI fallback needs reference context
  Parser -> Transition : Invoke supplied context callback:\nparserContext(sessionId, userId)
  Transition -> Sessions : snapshot(sessionId, userId)
  Sessions --> Transition : Read-only session snapshot
  Transition -> Transition : SessionContextProjector.project(snapshot)
  Transition --> Parser : Pending question, last action, displayed book ranks/titles
end
Parser --> Gateway : UserIntent
note over Parser
  Command fast paths do not load session context.
  The AI fallback receives only bounded reference context.
  Parser output does not decide final session behavior.
  Parser and response chat models can differ.
end note
Gateway -> Transition : Resolve and process UserIntent
Transition -> Sessions : update(sessionId, userId, change)
activate Sessions
note over Sessions
  Acquire session lock.
  Load session and run the transition.
end note
Sessions -> Transition : Apply change to loaded session
activate Transition
Transition -> Transition : IntentResolver.resolve(session, text, intent)\nCreate SessionRequest and apply session guardrails
Transition -> Engine : Resolve, validate and complete the turn
activate Engine

alt REPEAT
  Engine -> Engine : Restore LastOutcome\nKeep ActiveSearch unchanged
else EXPLAIN_PREFERENCES
  Engine -> Engine : Snapshot saved preferences and recommendation count\nKeep search, queue and pending question unchanged
else UPDATE_PREFERENCES
  Engine -> Engine : Merge additions/removals/replacements atomically\nRemove matching saved opposite semantic tastes
  note over Transition, Engine
    Category overflow is caught by SessionTransitionService.
    Keep saved preferences and the prior pending question;
    save a repeatable limit outcome instead of returning 400.
  end note
else Explanation or repeat recommendations
  Engine -> Engine : Reuse displayed page or saved outcome\nNo candidate retrieval
else MORE with no previous search
  Engine -> Engine : Mark search clarification required\nDo not retrieve candidates
else Recommendation, refinement, or MORE
  Engine -> Engine : Intent handler resolves context and preferences\nReplace ActiveSearch if search changes
  Engine -> History : Load current user's read IDs (bounded)
  History --> Engine : Read IDs, or logged fail-open on failure/oversize
  Engine -> Engine : Filter pending books against read/shown IDs\nTake up to requested count
  opt Page still needs books
    Engine -> Workflow : Build fresh batch, excluding read/shown IDs and cached tail
    activate Workflow
    Workflow -> Workflow : Load user preference vectors\nBuild query vectors when needed
    alt Personalised request lacks usable preferences
      Workflow --> Engine : Ask for taste preferences
    else Search can proceed
      Workflow -> Workflow : Retrieve up to 50 candidates\nRank up to 20 recommendations
      Workflow --> Engine : New batch for session queue
    end
    deactivate Workflow
    Engine -> Engine : Fill page from new queue\nReturn fewer if necessary
  end
  Engine -> Engine : Handler completes action; update LastOutcome\nEmpty MORE = no further matches
else Count, reset preferences, history, help, cancel or unknown action
  Engine -> Engine : Apply the relevant session action\nNo candidate retrieval
end

Engine --> Transition : Completed ConversationTurn
deactivate Engine
Transition --> Sessions : Transition result
deactivate Transition
Sessions -> Sessions : Commit session if lock and version still match\nKeep lease held and renewed
Sessions -> Gateway : Run afterCommit with selected page and decision
Gateway -> Response : Generate wording using resolved decision and context
note over Response
  Chat model for book explanations.
  Built-in wording for actions, clarification,
  exhausted results and model failures.
  Preference reports list all required/excluded constraints first,
  then styles, then genres/topics within the remaining word budget.
  Exact constraints are never truncated, including on REPEAT.
end note
Response --> Gateway : Response text
Gateway --> Sessions : Generated response
Sessions -> Sessions : Release session lease
Sessions --> Transition : Completed request
Transition --> Gateway : Generated response
deactivate Sessions
Gateway --> User : Response
note over Gateway, Sessions
  Commit precedes final response generation.
  Busy lock: 409. Lost lock or rejected commit: 503.
end note
@enduml
